From ccf85bc65d88adf4c63fd3541a2673ebe34e6703 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Andrey Borodin <amborodin@acm.org>
Date: Tue, 4 Aug 2026 21:48:21 +0500
Subject: [PATCH v1 1/2] Add B-tree support for specialized page searches

Binary search within a B-tree page repeatedly invokes the opclass
comparison function through fmgr and deforms each index tuple.  This is a
significant part of the cost of searches and random insertions for simple
fixed-width datatypes, where comparison itself is otherwise very cheap.

Add optional B-tree support procedure 7, which can install callbacks for
comparing an insertion key with a page tuple and for searching a complete
page interval.  An opclass callback can decline an individual operation, in
which case nbtree uses the existing generic implementation.

Use the facility for single-column int4 indexes.  The specialized callback
reads the fixed-width key directly and preserves nbtree's handling of NULLs,
descending order, pivot tuples, heap TID tie breakers, and posting lists.

The new procedure deliberately applies only when the scan key and index key
have the same type.  Cross-type searches continue to use the regular support
procedure 1 comparison function.
